    <bpmn:process id="W_W3792" name="W3792. Trade Compliance &amp; Sourcing Linkage (Tariff, Country, Sanctions)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Sourcing decision; trade-policy change
Frequency: Per decision + ongoing
Volume: All import sourcing decisions
Owner: Global Sourcing / Customs Compliance
Participants: Global Sourcing, Customs Compliance (links to VS-87), AML/Sanctions (links to VS-86), Legal (links to VS-100.3), Merchandising (links to VS-01), Finance (links to VS-17.4)
Source: workflow W3792 — Trade Compliance &amp; Sourcing Linkage (Tariff, Country, Sanctions)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3792_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3792_Lane1" name="Global Sourcing">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3792_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3792_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3792_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3792_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3792_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3792_Start3" name="Sourcing decision; trade-policy change">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3792_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3792_Task4" name="Global Sourcing/Customs embed trade compliance into sourcing decisions: HS/HTS…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Global Sourcing/Customs embed trade compliance into sourcing decisions: HS/HTS classification and duty impact per source country (links to VS-87), preferential-trade-agreement (PTA/FTA — e.g., ASEAN, ASEAN-China) utilization, anti-dumping/countervailing exposure, and country-of-origin rules — so sourcing is optimized for landed cost *after* duty
Responsible (R): Global Sourcing / Customs
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Per decision</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3792_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3792_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3792_Task5" name="Global Sourcing/AML screen all import vendors/agents/countries against…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Global Sourcing/AML screen all import vendors/agents/countries against sanctions and restricted-party lists (links to VS-86), manage trade-policy and sanctions monitoring, and block/re-route restricted sourcing
Responsible (R): Global Sourcing / AML / Compliance
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3792_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3792_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3792_Task6" name="Global Sourcing/Customs publish trade-compliance-informed sourcing analytics…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Global Sourcing/Customs publish trade-compliance-informed sourcing analytics (duty saved via PTA/FTA, anti-dumping exposure, sanctions screening coverage) to governance (links to W3808/VS-87)
Responsible (R): Global Sourcing / Customs / Finance
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3792_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3792_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3792_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3792_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-71 (ensure import sourcing &amp; social-compliance verification.) | - operational: compliance-informed sourcing; operational: screening (links to VS-86)
Owner: Global Sourcing / Customs Compliance</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
